  {"clause_id": "c002", "issues": [
    {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.07},
    {"issue": "Section 1 says the Employment Period ends \"as provided in Section 4\", but Section 4(a) fixes no term or expiry date while Section 4(b) speaks of termination \"during the term of this Agreement\". The gap leaves the duration of the instrument open to construction.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.18}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c003", "issues": [
    {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.11},
    {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.08}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c004", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Reasonable best efforts\", \"full business time\" and the carve-out for \"a reasonable amount of time to charitable or other similar activities\" set no measurable boundary, and the catch-all \"or other similar activities\" has uncertain reach against the enumerated \"charitable\".", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30},
    {"issue": "Section 9 (Other Businesses) forbids Employee from being \"engaged in, render[ing] services for, or permit[ting] his or her name to be used in connection with any business other than the business of the Company\", which is hard to square with 2(b)'s express permission to devote time to charitable or similar activities.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c005", "issues": [
    {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.13},
    {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.09}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c006", "issues": [
    {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.12},
    {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.09}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c007", "issues": [
    {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.10},
    {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.05}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c008", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The clause sets a commencement date but no ending date or renewal mechanism, so \"Term\" has no content beyond the listed termination events. Whether the Agreement is at-will indefinitely is left to construction.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22},
    {"issue": "Section 4(b) conditions severance on termination \"during the term of this Agreement\", but Section 4(a) never fixes any such term, so the two cannot be read together without supplying a term.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c009", "issues": [
    {"issue": "It is unclear whether \"entitled to receive his or her Base Salary ... during the twelve (12) month period\" means twelve months of salary continuation or something less, and the mitigation cut-off keyed to being \"employed ... on a full-time basis\" and to being \"in breach of Sections 5, 6 or 7\" (breach determined by whom, and on what standard) invites argument.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.44},
    {"issue": "Severance is payable only on termination \"during the term of this Agreement\", yet Section 4(a) fixes no term, leaving the condition precedent unanchored in the instrument.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c010", "issues": [
    {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.13},
    {"issue": "Section 4(c) limits an employee terminated for Cause or on resignation/death/Disability to \"only ... Base Salary through the date of termination\", while Section 20 promises the unpaid Sign-On Bonus in full on exactly those events. The two cannot both be applied literally.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.45}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c011", "issues": [
    {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.13},
    {"issue": "Section 4(d) cuts off all rights to \"bonuses ... and other compensation\" after termination except as provided in Section 4(b), but Section 20 expressly makes the unpaid Sign-On Bonus payable within 30 days after termination and Section 19 accelerates equity on a post-Change-of-Control termination.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.47}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c012", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Any physical or mental incapacitation which results in Employee's inability to perform his or her duties ... for a total of 120 days\" does not say whether partial incapacity counts, and the CEO's \"good faith judgment\" is the only measure. The deeming date in (ii) also assumes a continuous rather than aggregate 120 days.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.28},
    {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.08}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c013", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Clause (i) runs \"conviction of a felony or any other act or omission involving dishonesty, disloyalty or fraud\", so the general words sit against a criminal-conviction specific and their reach is uncertain, and (v) \"any other material breach of this Agreement\" is an open catch-all after four enumerated grounds. \"Conduct tending to bring the Company ... into substantial public disgrace or disrepute\" is also vague on its face.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.42},
    {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.10}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c014", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Confidential Information\" is defined as all \"information, observations and data ... concerning the business or affairs\" obtained while employed, with no time limit and no exclusion for the employee's general skill and knowledge, so its boundary against the public-domain proviso is contestable.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.34},
    {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.13}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c015", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Work Product\" covers anything relating to the Company's \"actual or anticipated business ... or existing or future products or services\", a boundary that cannot be fixed at the time of creation. The clause declares ownership rather than assigning, leaving the mechanism of transfer to construction.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24},
    {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.09}
  ]},
